WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.404
"You will be kind to visitors," Onatah's grandmother said.

2
00:00:12.405 --> 00:00:16.134
"These two can join the festival after Busk."

3
00:00:16.135 --> 00:00:20.808
She gave Onatah some old animal skins.

4
00:00:20.809 --> 00:00:23.473
"Put these in the fire."

5
00:00:23.474 --> 00:00:28.956
The children walked over to the large fire.

6
00:00:28.957 --> 00:00:32.403
"What is Busk?" Vinnie asked.

7
00:00:32.404 --> 00:00:39.280
"During the Green Corn Festival, we clean our homes completely," said Onatah.

8
00:00:39.281 --> 00:00:42.687
"We burn everything we do not use."

9
00:00:42.688 --> 00:00:47.010
Onatah threw the skins into the fire.

10
00:00:47.011 --> 00:00:49.759
People were staring at them.

11
00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.090
"Who are they?" asked one man.

12
00:00:53.091 --> 00:00:57.422
"Vinnie and Mandy," shrugged Onatah.

13
00:00:57.423 --> 00:01:01.213
"Grandmother welcomed them."

14
00:01:01.214 --> 00:01:05.545
"Then you are guests of the Onondaga," said the man.

15
00:01:05.546 --> 00:01:09.008
"Onondaga?" asked Mandy.

16
00:01:09.009 --> 00:01:11.811
The girl nodded proudly:

17
00:01:11.812 --> 00:01:16.133
"We are Onondaga, the People of the Hills.

18
00:01:16.134 --> 00:01:18.439
But Magua is Mohawk."

19
00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.951
She pointed to the man.

20
00:01:20.952 --> 00:01:27.684
"Five Indian nations make up the Iroquois, the People of the Longhouse," said Magua.

21
00:01:27.685 --> 00:01:30.173
He held up one hand.

22
00:01:30.174 --> 00:01:33.274
He counted five fingers:

23
00:01:33.275 --> 00:01:39.082
"Oneida, Cayuga, Onondaga, Seneca, and Mohawk."

24
00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:42.681
"Five nations?" asked Vinnie.

25
00:01:42.682 --> 00:01:47.124
"Yes, five nations became one people—the Iroquois!"

26
00:01:47.125 --> 00:01:51.807
said Magua, closing his hand into a fist.

27
00:01:51.808 --> 00:01:54.680
"Vinnie, do you like to fish?"

28
00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:57.887
"I've never tried it," said Vinnie.

29
00:01:57.888 --> 00:02:01.806
"I'll teach you how we fish," said Magua.

30
00:02:01.807 --> 00:02:06.149
"Is it safe to split up?" Mandy asked Vinnie.

31
00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:09.018
"It'll be fine," said Vinnie.

32
00:02:09.019 --> 00:02:11.361
He followed Magua.

33
00:02:11.362 --> 00:02:16.477
"Come," said Onatah, warming to her new friend.

34
00:02:16.478 --> 00:02:18.101
"I'll show you around.

35
00:02:18.102 --> 00:02:20.501
Then we'll go to my house."

36
00:02:20.502 --> 00:02:23.961
They walked past the longhouses.

37
00:02:23.962 --> 00:02:28.748
Mandy saw an animal sign above every door.

38
00:02:28.749 --> 00:02:32.615
"What do these signs mean?" she asked.

39
00:02:32.616 --> 00:02:36.327
"Iroquois people belong to different clans.

40
00:02:36.328 --> 00:02:44.759
Clans are like big families that grow from one woman born long ago," explained Onatah.

41
00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.695
"Every clan has its own longhouse.

42
00:02:47.696 --> 00:02:51.268
I belong to the Bear Clan."

43
00:02:51.269 --> 00:02:56.489
The girls arrived at Onatah's longhouse and went inside.

44
00:02:56.490 --> 00:03:01.255
"Let's make a corn husk doll," suggested Onatah.

45
00:03:01.256 --> 00:03:05.672
She gave Mandy some corn hanging from the ceiling.

46
00:03:05.673 --> 00:03:12.103
Mandy also saw floor mats made from corn husks.

47
00:03:12.104 --> 00:03:16.667
"Is corn your main crop?" Mandy asked.

48
00:03:16.668 --> 00:03:23.095
"It is one of three vegetables we call the Three Sisters," Onatah replied.

49
00:03:23.096 --> 00:03:29.748
"Beans, squash, and corn must grow together as sisters do."

50
00:03:29.749 --> 00:03:33.407
Mandy and Onatah husked the corn.

51
00:03:33.408 --> 00:03:38.887
"Let's get some beaver skin for a doll dress," said Onatah.

52
00:03:38.888 --> 00:03:42.805
The girls ran out the door.

53
00:03:42.806 --> 00:03:46.812
Vinnie and Magua got into a canoe.

54
00:03:46.813 --> 00:03:51.200
They paddled out on a nearby stream.

55
00:03:51.201 --> 00:03:55.004
"This is for you," said Magua.

56
00:03:55.005 --> 00:04:02.160
He gave Vinnie a long spear that was in the canoe.

57
00:04:02.161 --> 00:04:04.858
"You catch fish with this?"

58
00:04:04.859 --> 00:04:08.601
asked Vinnie, looking at his spear.

59
00:04:08.602 --> 00:04:11.559
"Watch," smiled Magua.

60
00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:17.765
He carefully aimed his spear and quickly pierced a fish.

61
00:04:17.766 --> 00:04:20.581
"Wow!" yelled Vinnie.

62
00:04:20.582 --> 00:04:23.502
"Is this how everyone does it?"

63
00:04:23.503 --> 00:04:28.528
"Only when we fish alone or with a friend," said Magua.

64
00:04:28.529 --> 00:04:32.023
"Mostly, we use the fish traps we've built."

65
00:04:32.024 --> 00:04:35.204
"Fish traps?" asked Vinnie.

66
00:04:35.205 --> 00:04:38.105
"The stream guides the fish into the trap,"

67
00:04:38.106 --> 00:04:44.541
said Magua, pointing to a large circular dam made out of sticks.

68
00:04:44.542 --> 00:04:47.493
"Then we use a net to catch them."

69
00:04:47.494 --> 00:04:52.098
"Why are you in the Onondaga village?" asked Vinnie.

70
00:04:52.099 --> 00:04:53.872
"I am only visiting.

71
00:04:53.873 --> 00:04:58.474
My people live toward the rising sun," said Magua.

72
00:04:58.475 --> 00:05:01.477
"We are the Keepers of the Eastern Door.

73
00:05:01.478 --> 00:05:05.347
Mohawks protect the Iroquois from the whites in the East."

74
00:05:05.348 --> 00:05:10.015
Raising his spear, Magua moved with great speed.

75
00:05:10.016 --> 00:05:19.450
Then he speared another big fish.
